## Three questions, three pages

**Grow: what could my savings become?** Type what you'd save and how often, choose how it's invested, and watch it compound. The numbers come from real S&P 500, TSX and savings returns since 1970. 2,000 simulated market paths give a rough, a typical and a great outcome, and a toggle shows it all in today's dollars.

{% Figure
   src="/media/meet-wealthwego/grow.webp"
   alt="Grow page: $300 a month grows to a typical $66,891 in ten years"
   caption="Grow: $300 a month, ten years, real market history." /%}

**Budget: where does my money go?** List income and spending as they really arrive: every two weeks, monthly, yearly. You see what's left each month, the share each spending takes, when a car lease ends and frees up $420, and what your savings grow into.

It also builds in the book's favourite idea: **room for error**. Pick a cushion of three to twelve months of essentials. The app fills it first, then shows how the rest compounds.

{% Figure
   src="/media/meet-wealthwego/budget.webp"
   alt="Budget page: $4,983 in, $3,188 out, $1,795 left over each month"
   caption="Budget: what's left each month, and where every dollar goes." /%}

**Rule: how close am I to a famous rule?** Pick one of seven well-known rules, such as 50/30/20 or pay yourself first, and see exactly how far your own budget is from it, in dollars a month.

{% Figure
   src="/media/meet-wealthwego/rule.webp"
   alt="Rule page: a budget compared with 50/30/20, row by row"
   caption="Rule: your budget next to 50/30/20, line by line." /%}

## What it doesn't do

WealthWeGo doesn't connect to your bank, sell you products or tell you which fund to buy. It's a planner, not financial advice.

It also doesn't need to know who you are. Without an account, your plan never leaves your browser. If you'd like it on your phone and your laptop, sign in with Google and it syncs, encrypted.

## Try it

Type what you could save each month and watch it grow. No sign-up, no bank login.

[**Try WealthWeGo →**](https://wealthwego.siiulan.dev)

